Displacement of the free end of a submaximally-activated cat soleus muscle
relative to its initial position, with a maximum amplitude of 8.0 mm.
Experimental data was provided by T.G. Sandercock [1]. Please refer to Millard
et al. [2] for details.

References:
    1. Perreault, E.J., Heckman, C.J., and Sandercock, T.G., 2003. "Hill
       muscle model errors during movement are greatest within the
       physiologically relevant range of motor unit firing rates". Journal
       of Biomechanics, 36(2), pp. 211--218.
       http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/S0021-9290(02)00332-9.
    2. Millard, M., Uchida, T., Seth, A., and Delp, S.L., 2013. "Flexing
       computational muscle: Modeling and simulation of musculotendon
       dynamics". ASME Journal of Biomechanical Engineering, 135(2),
       p. 021013 (11 pages). http://dx.doi.org/10.1115/1.4023390.

